index c09c903..76b8cd7 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1 +1,95 @@
+# bin — personal script collection
+
 - bin dir in my home folder
+
+## Layout
+
+The Python scripts are **folderized by functionality**: every script that does the same job
+as another one lives in the same sub-directory (e.g. all Zstandard compressors in
+`compress_zstd/`, all "strip comments from Python files" tools in `strip_comments_python/`,
+all wheel repackers in `wheel_build_repack/`).
+
+- 161 folders, 1204 scripts grouped + 5 scripts in the repo root = **1209 scripts**.
+- A folder is only created when it has **at least two members**; scripts with a unique job
+  stay in the repo root: `cli_wrapper.py`, `fix_html_md_broken_links.py`,
+  `gitignore_updater.py`, `rm_from_archive.py`, `update_summary.py`.
+- The old extension-less symlinks that mirrored each `*.py` name
+  (`20most -> .../bin/20most.py`) were removed; they pointed at absolute Termux paths and
+  were broken duplicates of the script names.
+- Every script parses under **Python 3.11** as well as 3.12/3.13 (`compileall .` is clean).
+
+Full folder → script listing, plus the duplicate report: **[SCRIPT_INDEX.md](SCRIPT_INDEX.md)**
+
+The tooling that produced this layout — the feature dump and folderizer from step 1, the
+duplicate scanner, the PEP 701 f-string fixer, the index generator and the test battery
+for the merged scripts — lives in **[arena/](arena/README.md)** and is excluded from the
+index and the scans.
+
+Folders are sorted by size in that index, so the biggest clusters (the ones with the most
+overlap) come first.
+
+## Duplicate collapse
+
+Two content-similarity passes (whitespace/shebang-normalised `difflib` ratio over every pair
+inside a folder) found 21 pairs ≥ 95 % and then 18 pairs ≥ 90 % similar. All but three were
+collapsed into one canonical script each — **34 scripts removed, 5 merged scripts added**.
+
+### Round 1 — pairs ≥ 95 %
+
+- **9 redundant twins deleted** — the better copy was kept (e.g. `annotate_types.py` →
+  `add_typing.py`, `cleanmd.py` → `markdown_image_remover.py`, `fssim.py`/`ssdim.py` →
+  `ssim2.py`, `dduper.py` → `deduplicate_python.py`).
+- **2 opposite-job pairs resolved** — `jb2.py` (JSON beautify) and `bcss.py` (CSS beautify)
+  were dropped in favour of the minifiers; pretty-printing still lives in
+  `code_beautify_prettier/` (`prettify.py`, `pret3.py`, `pypret.py`).
+- **3 template families merged into one parameterised script**:
+  - `extract_python_entities/ex_nodes.py --kind class|func|docstrings|comments|all`
+    (replaces `ex_class.py`, `ex_func.py`, `ex_ex.py`, `ex_comments.py`)
+  - `font_convert/font_convert.py --to woff|woff2|ttf [-r]`
+    (replaces `otf2woff2.py`, `ttf2woff2.py`, `woff2woff2.py`, `woff22woff.py`)
+  - `cli_wrapper.py <binary> …` / `--bin /path/to/bin`
+    (replaces `cli_wrapper_log/feloai.py`, `cli_wrapper_log/wrapper_gh.py`)
+
+### Round 2 — pairs ≥ 90 %
+
+- **5 superseded variants deleted** — `extar.py` → `ex_tar.py` (safe `filter="data"`),
+  `imz.py` → `imz2.py`, `afkco.py` → `afk.py`, `mk_stand.py`/`mkst.py` → `inline_assets.py`,
+  and `gext2.py` replaced `gext.py` (then took over its name).
+- **7 families merged into one parameterised script**:
+  - `find_files_by_time/files_by_time.py --order newest|oldest [--time mtime|ctime|atime] [-r] [-n N]`
+    (replaces `newest_files.py`, `oldest_files.py`)
+  - `archive_convert_codec/convert_gz_xz.py [--to auto|xz|gz] [--dry-run]`
+    (replaces `gz2xz.py`, `xz2gz.py`; direction comes from each file's extension)
+  - `ls_dir_listing/l.py [-r|--reverse] [N]` (replaces `lll.py`)
+  - `html_md_convert/html_to_md.py --engine html2text|markdownify [--keep]` (replaces `tomd.py`)
+  - `minify_web_assets/mincss.py --engine csso|cleancss` (replaces `ccss.py`)
+  - `translate_dict_json/mendic.py --direction en2fa|fa2en [--keep]` (replaces `mfadic.py`)
+  - `scrape_site_links/findlinks.py URL [EXT] [MAX_PAGES] [DELAY]` (replaces `findpdflinks.py`)
+- **Bugs fixed while merging** — `gz2xz.py` called `get_files()` without importing it;
+  both gz↔xz converters `stat()`ed the source *after* deleting it, so every ratio and the
+  "space saved" summary were always 0; `newest_files.py` and `oldest_files.py` printed each
+  other's header; `findlinks.py` died with a `NameError` on scheme-less URLs
+  (`urlparse(url)` → `urlparse(start_url)`) and printed `None` as its usage text;
+  `l.py` parsed `-r` into a variable it never used.
+
+### Still ≥ 90 % similar, kept on purpose
+
+Same shape of code, genuinely different jobs — collapsing them would lose functionality:
+
+| pair | similarity | why both stay |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `minify_web_assets/pcssmin.py` ↔ `pjsmin.py` | 92.6 % | CSS vs JavaScript |
+| `strip_comments_web/clean_css.py` ↔ `cleants.py` | 91.6 % | tree-sitter CSS vs TypeScript grammar |
+| `translate_code_comments/pytrans.py` ↔ `pytranslator.py` | 90.3 % | pycld2 vs langdetect detection engines |
+
+## Python 3.11 compatibility
+
+31 scripts parsed only on Python 3.12+: `ruff format` with `target-version = "py312"`
+(see `pyproject.toml`) splits a long f-string **expression** over several physical lines,
+which is PEP 701 syntax. Those expressions were joined back onto one line — a
+whitespace-only change inside `{...}`, so the rendered strings are byte-identical — except in
+`html_template_gen/make_template_html.py`, where the table-of-contents generator moved out of
+the f-string into a `toc` variable. `python3 -m compileall .` is now clean on 3.11.
+
+Running `ruff format` again with `target-version = "py312"` will split them again; set
+`target-version = "py311"` in `pyproject.toml` if the compatibility should survive formatting.
